{"availability":"available","full":"nksaraf/magiql","name":"magiql","description":"🌐 💫 Simple and powerful GraphQL Client, love child of react-query ❤️ relay ","category":"Developer tools","language":"TypeScript","stars":200,"forks":1,"created":"2020-04-04T11:31:56Z","updated":"2021-12-31T03:05:22Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://magiql.vercel.app","topics":["babel-plugin","codegen","data-fetching","graphql","graphql-client","magic","react","react-query","recoiljs","relay","relay-hooks"],"demo":"https://magiql.vercel.app/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-06T21:08:00.463Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-06T21:08:00.463Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-06T21:08:00.463Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-06T21:08:00.463Z","stars":200,"forks":1}],"technologies":["React"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A bunch of simple but magical React hooks to work with GraphQL. powered by react-query, inspired by relay and urql","A set of React hooks to work with GraphQL data. magiql stands on the shoulders of massive giants in the data-synchronization and state-management space, both conceputally and some as actual dependencies. It uses the amazing react-query library as its data-fetching and synchronization layer which forms the foundation of this library. Seriously, without react-query, this won't be any good. The API is also very similar to react-query and will be familiar to the users. It's just slightly tweaked to make it easier to work with GraphQL. On top of the these great synchronization primitives, we add…","magiql is designed to be easy to adopt (moving from vanilla react-query or other GraphQL clients). Most features (like normalized caching, recoil-based store implementation, relay-compiler and build-time optimizations) are completely optional and configurable. But everything is included under one installed dependency so that you don't have to install things again and again (don't worry, the different entry-points are code-split and you will only include things that you actually use). You can start using magiql as a GraphQL Client immediately and it grows to cater to your needs as they arise…"],"features":["Most of the features that we are providing are thanks to react-query. Using inspiration from relay and urql, we are able to provide a bunch of additional awesome GraphQL-specific features that you can find below","Auto Caching + Refetching (stale-while-revalidate, Window Refocus, Polling/Realtime)","Parallel + Dependent Queries","Request Deduplication","Paginated + Cursor-based Queries"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/nksaraf/magiql/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"de9eb627af8d70d158f33fa7e54a5a564d1cd53d64b182876cf0f0f3672226cd","extractedAt":"2026-10-06T21:08:00.601Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-06T21:08:00.601Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A bunch of simple but magical React hooks to work with GraphQL. powered by react-query, inspired by relay and urql","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/nksaraf/magiql/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"de9eb627af8d70d158f33fa7e54a5a564d1cd53d64b182876cf0f0f3672226cd","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/nksaraf/magiql/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-06T21:08:00.602Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2021-12-31T03:05:22Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/nksaraf/magiql/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-06T21:08:00.604Z","hash":"de9eb627af8d70d158f33fa7e54a5a564d1cd53d64b182876cf0f0f3672226cd","originalBytes":20342,"storedBytes":20342,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["magiql","graphql","import","react","queries","data","fragments","query","person","relay","graphqlclient","react-query","using","caching","const","name","normalized","babel","features","relay-compiler","add","compiler","refetching","return","support","api","client","entities","generated","tsx","usequery","work","component","components","entity","new","store","these",